pe=heads \"SECURITY.md\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> TESTING.md  ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/TESTING.md?ref_type=heads \"TESTING.md\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> docs.Dockerfile  ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/docs.Dockerfile?ref_type=heads \"docs.Dockerfile\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> janusgraph.png  ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/janusgraph.png?ref_type=heads \"janusgraph.png\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> mkdocs.yml  ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/mkdocs.yml?ref_type=heads \"mkdocs.yml\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> pom.xml  ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/pom.xml?ref_type=heads \"pom.xml\") |  |   \\n[ <::before> requirements.txt  ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/requirements.txt?ref_type=heads \"requirements.txt\") |  |   \\n  \\n[ **README.md** ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/README.md?ref_type=heads)\\n\\n[ ](https://janusgraph.org/)\\n\\nJanusGraph is a highly scalable [ graph database ](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_database) optimized for storing and querying large graphs with billions of vertices and edges distributed across a multi-machine cluster. JanusGraph is a transactional database that can support thousands of concurrent users, complex traversals, and analytic graph queries. \\n\\n[ ](https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/releases) [ ](https://hub.docker.com/r/janusgraph/janusgraph) [ ](https://central.sonatype.com/search?q=org.janusgraph) [ ](https://javadoc.io/doc/org.janusgraph/janusgraph-core) [ ](https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/actions) [ ](https://codecov.io/gh/JanusGraph/janusgraph) [ ](https://github.com/zrosenbauer/awesome-bigtable) [ ](https://bestpractices.coreinfrastructure.org/projects/5064) [ ](https://www.codacy.com/gh/JanusGraph/janusgraph/dashboard?utm_source=github.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=JanusGraph/janusgraph&utm_campaign=Badge_Grade)\\n\\n##  <::after> Learn More \\n\\nThe [ project homepage ](https://janusgraph.org) contains more information on JanusGraph and provides links to documentation, getting-started guides and release downloads. \\n\\n##  <::after> Visualization \\n\\nTo visualize graphs stored in JanusGraph, you can use any of the following tools: \\n\\n  * <::marker> [ Arcade Analytics ](https://arcadeanalytics.com/usermanual/#arcade-analytics)\\n  * <::marker> [ Cytoscape ](https://www.cytoscape.org/)\\n  * <::marker> [ Gephi ](https://tinkerpop.apache.org/docs/current/reference/#gephi-plugin) plugin for Apache TinkerPop \\n  * <::marker> [ Graphexp ](https://github.com/bricaud/graphexp)\\n  * <::marker> [ Graph Explorer ](https://github.com/invanalabs/graph-explorer)\\n  * <::marker> [ Graphlytic ](https://graphlytic.com/)\\n  * <::marker> [ Gremlin-Visualizer ](https://github.com/prabushitha/gremlin-visualizer)\\n  * <::marker> [ G.V() - Gremlin IDE ](https://gdotv.com)\\n  * <::marker> [ KeyLines by Cambridge Intelligence ](https://cambridge-intelligence.com/keylines/janusgraph/)\\n  * <::marker> [ Ogma by Linkurious ](https://doc.linkurious.com/ogma/latest/tutorials/janusgraph/)\\n  * <::marker> [ ReGraph by Cambridge Intelligence ](https://cambridge-intelligence.com/regraph/)\\n  * <::marker> [ Tom Sawyer Perspectives ](https://www.tomsawyer.com/perspectives/)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Community \\n\\n  * <::marker>\\n\\nGitHub Discussions: see [ ` GitHub Discussions ` ](https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph/discussions) for all general discussions and questions about JanusGraph \\n\\n  * <::marker>\\n\\nDiscord for interactive discussions and questions about JanusGraph: [ Join the server ](https://discord.gg/5n4fjv4QAf)\\n\\n  * <::marker>\\n\\nStack Overflow: see the [ ` janusgraph ` ](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/janusgraph) tag \\n\\n  * <::marker>\\n\\nTwitter: follow [ @JanusGraph ](https://twitter.com/JanusGraph) for news and updates \\n\\n  * <::marker>\\n\\nLinkedIn: follow [ JanusGraph ](https://www.linkedin.com/company/janusgraph) for news and updates \\n\\n  * <::marker>\\n\\nMailing lists: \\n\\n    * <::marker>\\n\\n**janusgraph-users (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation** ( [ archives ](https://lists.lfaidata.foundation/g/janusgraph-users/topics) ) for questions about using JanusGraph, installation, configuration, integrations \\n\\nTo join with a LF AI & Data account, use the [ web UI ](https://lists.lfaidata.foundation/g/janusgraph-users/join) ; to subscribe/unsubscribe with an arbitrary email address, send an email to: \\n\\n      * <::marker>janusgraph-users+subscribe (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation \\n      * <::marker>janusgraph-users+unsubscribe (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation \\n    * <::marker>\\n\\n**janusgraph-dev (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation** ( [ archives ](https://lists.lfaidata.foundation/g/janusgraph-dev/topics) ) for internal implementation of JanusGraph itself \\n\\nTo join with a LF AI & Data account, use the [ web UI ](https://lists.lfaidata.foundation/g/janusgraph-dev/join) ; to subscribe/unsubscribe with an arbitrary email address, send an email to: \\n\\n      * <::marker>janusgraph-dev+subscribe (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation \\n      * <::marker>janusgraph-dev+unsubscribe (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation \\n    * <::marker>\\n\\n**janusgraph-announce (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation** ( [ archives ](https://lists.lfaidata.foundation/g/janusgraph-announce/topics) ) for new releases and news announcements \\n\\nTo join with a LF AI & Data account, use the [ web UI ](https://lists.lfaidata.foundation/g/janusgraph-announce/join) ; to subscribe/unsubscribe with an arbitrary email address, send an email to: \\n\\n      * <::marker>janusgraph-announce+subscribe (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation \\n      * <::marker>janusgraph-announce+unsubscribe (at) lists.lfaidata.foundation \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Contributing \\n\\nPlease see [ ` CONTRIBUTING.md ` ](/root/janusgraph/-/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md) for more information, including CLAs and best practices for working with GitHub. \\n\\n##  <::after> Powered by JanusGraph \\n\\n  * <::marker> [ Apache Atlas ](https://github.